>> Laugh() and of Sneeze() have the same value): specifically, the challenge
>> is to represent that in a concise and human-usable way (bearing in mind
>> that a normal sentence might involve dozens of groups of argument-places
>> that have the same value). You c
>> >     ould call this loglang "LoCCan3", but, unlike John Clifford's
>> vision, it couldn't be achieved by incremental revisions to LoCCan2.
>> >
>> > I can praise any improvements backward compatible with the current
